{"id":"e07t2","name":"Consumption from Counters","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["spark","readings_df"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>Smart meters send the value of a <b>cumulative</b> counter (in kWh) several times a day. <code>readings_df</code> has the columns <code>meter_id</code> (string), <code>read_at</code> (timestamp) and <code>counter</code> (double, can be <code>null</code> when the meter could not read it).</p>\n<p>The consumption between two consecutive valid readings of the same meter (ordered by <code>read_at</code>) is computed like this:</p>\n<ul><li>readings with a <code>null</code> counter are ignored; if a meter sends several readings with the same <code>read_at</code>, only the one with the <b>highest</b> counter is kept;</li><li>normally, the consumption is <code>counter - previous counter</code>;</li><li>if the counter is <b>lower</b> than the previous one, the meter was reset to <code>0</code>: the consumption is the new <code>counter</code> itself;</li><li>the first valid reading of a meter has no consumption.</li></ul>\n<p>The consumption is assigned to the <b>day of the later reading</b>. Your task is to return, for every meter and day that has at least one consumption, the columns <code>meter_id</code>, <code>day</code> (date), <code>kwh</code> (double, rounded to 3 decimals) and <code>resets</code> (long, the number of resets detected that day), sorted by <code>meter_id</code>, then <code>day</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p><code>readings_df</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>meter_id</th><th>read_at</th><th>counter</th></tr><tr><td>m1</td><td>2026-03-01 00:00:00</td><td>100.0</td></tr><tr><td>m1</td><td>2026-03-01 12:00:00</td><td>104.5</td></tr><tr><td>m1</td><td>2026-03-01 18:00:00</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>m1</td><td>2026-03-02 06:00:00</td><td>2.0</td></tr><tr><td>m1</td><td>2026-03-02 12:00:00</td><td>3.25</td></tr><tr><td>m2</td><td>2026-03-01 23:00:00</td><td>50.0</td></tr><tr><td>m2</td><td>2026-03-02 01:00:00</td><td>51.0</td></tr><tr><td>m2</td><td>2026-03-02 01:00:00</td><td>50.5</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>meter_id</th><th>day</th><th>kwh</th><th>resets</th></tr><tr><td>m1</td><td>2026-03-01</td><td>4.5</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>m1</td><td>2026-03-02</td><td>3.25</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>m2</td><td>2026-03-02</td><td>1.0</td><td>0</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB</div>","starter":"from pyspark.sql import SparkSession, DataFrame, functions as F\nfrom pyspark.sql.window import Window\n\n\ndef solve(spark: SparkSession, readings_df: DataFrame) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return readings_df\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["lag","remise à zéro du compteur","doublons","agrégat par jour"],"minutes":20,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"readings_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"meter_id string, read_at timestamp, counter double","rows":[["m1","2026-03-01 00:00:00",100.0],["m1","2026-03-01 12:00:00",104.5],["m1","2026-03-01 18:00:00",null],["m1","2026-03-02 06:00:00",2.0],["m1","2026-03-02 12:00:00",3.25],["m2","2026-03-01 23:00:00",50.0],["m2","2026-03-02 01:00:00",51.0],["m2","2026-03-02 01:00:00",50.5]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["meter_id","day","kwh","resets"],"rows":[["m1","2026-03-01",4.5,0],["m1","2026-03-02",3.25,1],["m2","2026-03-02",1.0,0]]}},{"input":{"readings_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"meter_id string, read_at timestamp, counter double","rows":[["z","2026-01-01 00:00:00",10.0],["z","2026-01-01 00:00:00",null],["y","2026-01-01 00:00:00",5.0],["z","2026-01-02 00:00:00",4.0]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["meter_id","day","kwh","resets"],"rows":[["z","2026-01-02",4.0,1]]}}],"hidden_n":6,"hidden":"","solution":""}